            "ref": "word/document.xml#p0030",
            "textSha256": "53420047544e125fa6adbeaf60101673702795576c5fc3e3a8f98b9d07d73ea8"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we will explore the city of Sucre, which preserves its colonial and republican buildings, part of Bolivia's history. Sucre was named \"Cultural Heritage of Humanity\" (1991 by UNESCO). Visit the main attractions, including Plaza de Armas, the Cathedral, the Basilica of San Francisco Javier, the House of Freedom, the Asur Textile Museum, and the Recoleta Museum. On the slopes of Cerro Churuquella with an incredible view of the city, then return to the hotel."
    },
